WEBVTT

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:04.180
Once upon a time there were three Bears,
who lived together in a house of

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:05.420
their own, in a wood.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.240
One of them was a Little Wee Bear, and one
was a Middle-sized Bear, and the

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.180
other was a Great Big Bear.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.200
They had each a bowl for their porridge;

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.990
a little bowl for the Little Wee Bear;

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.420
and a middle-sized bowl for the
Middle-sized Bear;

00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:25.420
and a great bowl for the Great Big Bear.

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:28.240
And they had each a chair to sit in;

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.160
a little chair for the Little Wee Bear;

00:00:31.610 --> 00:00:34.570
and a middle-sized chair for the
Middle-sized Bear;

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:37.520
and a great chair for the Great Big Bear.

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:40.340
And they had each a bed to sleep in;

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.120
a little bed for the Little Wee Bear;

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:46.610
and a middle-sized bed for the
Middle-sized Bear;

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:49.560
and a great bed for the Great Big Bear.

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:54.220
One day, after they had made the porridge
for their breakfast, and poured it

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:58.260
into their porridge-bowls, they walked out
into the wood while the porridge

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:03.080
was cooling, that they might not burn
their mouths by beginning too soon, for

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:06.000
they were polite, well-brought-up Bears.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.580
And while they were away a little girl
called Goldilocks, who lived at the

00:01:10.580 --> 00:01:15.370
other side of the wood and had been sent
on an errand by her mother, passed by

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:17.690
the house, and looked in at the window.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:22.840
And then she peeped in at the keyhole, for
she was not at all a well-brought-

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.840
up little girl. Then seeing nobody in the
house she lifted the latch.

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:33.110
The door was not fastened, because the
Bears were good Bears, who did nobody

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:36.880
any harm, and never suspected that anybody
would harm them.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:40.160
So Goldilocks opened the door and went in;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.170
and well pleased was she when she saw the
porridge on the table.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:48.730
If she had been a well-brought-up little
girl she would have waited till the

00:01:48.730 --> 00:01:53.320
Bears came home, and then, perhaps, they
would have asked her to breakfast;

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:59.100
for they were good Bears—a little rough or
so, as the manner of Bears is, but

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:02.500
for all that very good-natured and
hospitable.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:07.880
But she was an impudent, rude little girl,
and so she set about helping

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.750
herself. First she tasted the porridge of
the Great Big Bear, and that was

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:12.580
too hot for her.

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:16.920
Next she tasted the porridge of the
Middle-sized Bear, but that was too cold

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.430
for her. And then she went to the porridge
of the Little Wee Bear, and tasted

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:26.570
it, and that was neither too hot nor too
cold, but just right, and she liked

00:02:26.570 --> 00:02:29.590
it so well that she ate it all up, every
bit!

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:34.050
Then Goldilocks, who was tired, for she
had been catching butterflies instead

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:38.720
of running on her errand, sat down in the
chair of the Great Big Bear, but

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.060
that was too hard for her.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:44.840
And then she sat down in the chair of the
Middle-sized Bear, and that was too

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:49.950
soft for her. But when she sat down in the
chair of the Little Wee Bear, that

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:53.620
was neither too hard nor too soft, but
just right.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:58.470
So she seated herself in it, and there she
sat till the bottom of the chair

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:02.180
came out, and down she came, plump upon
the ground;

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:06.670
and that made her very cross, for she was
a bad-tempered little girl.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.820
Now, being determined to rest, Goldilocks
went upstairs into the bedchamber in

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.250
which the Three Bears slept.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:18.160
And first she lay down upon the bed of the
Great Big Bear, but that was too

00:03:18.160 --> 00:03:19.330
high at the head for her.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:24.390
And next she lay down upon the bed of the
Middle-sized Bear, and that was too

00:03:24.390 --> 00:03:25.530
high at the foot for her.

00:03:26.110 --> 00:03:30.060
And then she lay down upon the bed of the
Little Wee Bear, and that was

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:33.370
neither too high at the head nor at the
foot, but just right.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:38.620
So she covered herself up comfortably, and
lay there till she fell fast asleep.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:42.390
By this time the Three Bears thought their
porridge would be cool enough for

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:43.600
them to eat it properly;

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:45.690
so they came home to breakfast.

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.590
Now careless Goldilocks had left the spoon
of the Great Big Bear standing in

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:53.580
his porridge. "SOMEBODY HAS BEEN AT MY
PORRIDGE!"

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.870
said the Great Big Bear in his great,
rough, gruff voice.

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:00.780
Then the Middle-sized Bear looked at his
porridge and saw the spoon was

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:01.870
standing in it too. "

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.160
SOMEBODY HAS BEEN AT MY PORRIDGE!"

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:07.090
said the Middle-sized Bear in his
middle-sized voice.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:10.970
Then the Little Wee Bear looked at his,
and there was the spoon in the

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:14.090
porridge-bowl, but the porridge was all
gone! "

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.680
SOMEBODY HAS BEEN AT MY PORRIDGE, AND HAS
EATEN IT ALL UP!"

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:20.320
said the Little Wee Bear in his little wee
voice.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:24.060
Upon this the Three Bears, seeing that
some one had entered their house, and

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:27.130
eaten up the Little Wee Bear's breakfast,
began to look about them.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:31.550
Now the careless Goldilocks had not put
the hard cushion straight when she

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.490
rose from the chair of the Great Big Bear.
"

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.680
SOMEBODY HAS BEEN SITTING IN MY CHAIR!"

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:39.690
said the Great Big Bear in his great,
rough, gruff voice.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:44.260
And the careless Goldilocks had squatted
down the soft cushion of the Middle-

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:48.230
sized Bear. "SOMEBODY HAS BEEN SITTING IN
MY CHAIR!"

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.120
said the Middle-sized Bear in his
middle-sized voice. "

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:56.030
SOMEBODY HAS BEEN SITTING IN MY CHAIR, AND
HAS SAT THE BOTTOM THROUGH!"

00:04:56.260 --> 00:04:58.650
said the Little Wee Bear in his little wee
voice.

00:04:59.670 --> 00:05:03.110
Then the Three Bears thought they had
better make further search in case it

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:06.720
was a burglar, so they went upstairs into
their bedchamber.

00:05:07.310 --> 00:05:11.610
Now Goldilocks had pulled the pillow of
the Great Big Bear out of its place. "

00:05:12.190 --> 00:05:14.660
SOMEBODY HAS BEEN LYING IN MY BED!"

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:18.360
said the Great Big Bear in his great,
rough, gruff voice.

00:05:18.930 --> 00:05:22.980
And Goldilocks had pulled the bolster of
the Middle-sized Bear out of its

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:26.550
place. "SOMEBODY HAS BEEN LYING IN MY
BED!"

00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:29.710
said the Middle-sized Bear in his
middle-sized voice.

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:34.830
But when the Little Wee Bear came to look
at his bed, there was the bolster in

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:38.780
its place! And the pillow was in its place
upon the bolster!

00:05:39.210 --> 00:05:40.360
And upon the pillow——?

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:45.950
There was Goldilocks's yellow head—which
was not in its place, for she had no

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:51.550
business there. "SOMEBODY HAS BEEN LYING
IN MY BED,—AND HERE SHE IS STILL!"

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:54.630
said the Little Wee Bear in his little wee
voice.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:59.020
Now Goldilocks had heard in her sleep the
great, rough, gruff voice of the

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:03.640
Great Big Bear; but she was so fast asleep
that it was no more to her than the

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:06.160
roaring of wind, or the rumbling of
thunder.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:10.920
And she had heard the middle-sized voice
of the Middle-sized Bear, but it was

00:06:10.920 --> 00:06:13.980
only as if she had heard some one speaking
in a dream.

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.770
But when she heard the little wee voice of
the Little Wee Bear, it was so

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:22.220
sharp, and so shrill, that it awakened her
at once.

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:27.380
Up she started, and when she saw the Three
Bears on one side of the bed, she

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:30.460
tumbled herself out at the other, and ran
to the window.

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:35.600
Now the window was open, because the
Bears, like good, tidy Bears, as they

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:39.730
were, always opened their bedchamber
window when they got up in the morning.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:43.030
So naughty, frightened little Goldilocks
jumped;

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:47.620
and whether she broke her neck in the
fall, or ran into the wood and was lost

00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:51.900
there, or found her way out of the wood
and got whipped for being a bad girl

00:06:51.900 --> 00:06:54.320
and playing truant, no one can say.

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:58.100
But the Three Bears never saw anything
more of her.
